Build your muscles!

79
00:12:16,039 --> 00:12:17,519
Ready to take a hit!

80
00:12:25,360 --> 00:12:26,840
Train your body!

81
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:29,720
Stay ready!

82
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:32,720
Build your muscles!

83
00:12:33,639 --> 00:12:34,399
Ready to take a hit!

84
00:12:35,679 --> 00:12:37,399
The members of our Special Police Unit

85
00:12:37,639 --> 00:12:39,519
have unmatched physical fitness.

86
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:42,159
I lost sight of you halfway through the run.

87
00:12:42,559 --> 00:12:43,879
I had to push myself so hard

88
00:12:43,879 --> 00:12:44,960
just to catch up with you.

89
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:45,799
Not bad.

90
00:12:46,279 --> 00:12:47,279
You pushed through.

91
00:12:48,080 --> 00:12:49,120
With a determined heart,

92
00:12:49,519 --> 00:12:51,039
anything is possible.

93
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:52,879
Perseverance.

94
00:12:54,279 --> 00:12:55,080
That is very important.

95
00:12:56,399 --> 00:12:58,240
Hope Commissar Tan has it every day.

96
00:13:00,879 --> 00:13:01,320
Dismissed!

97
00:13:06,360 --> 00:13:06,879
Commissar Tan,

98
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:08,159
you owe me breakfast.

99
00:13:08,440 --> 00:13:09,159
I ran with you yesterday,

100
00:13:09,159 --> 00:13:09,879
and didn't even get to eat.

101
00:13:11,039 --> 00:13:12,120
Doesn't the cafeteria have food?

102
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:12,720
Who's treating?

103
00:13:14,480 --> 00:13:15,480
I can treat you to a midnight snack.

104
00:13:21,639 --> 00:13:22,879
You can't do this, Mingming.

105
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:24,639
I bought you new clothes,

106
00:13:24,639 --> 00:13:25,639
and bought you a chicken cutlet.

107
00:13:26,200 --> 00:13:27,399
How can you just change your mind like that?

108
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:29,480
You...

109
00:13:30,759 --> 00:13:31,840
You lied to me!

110
00:13:32,799 --> 00:13:33,840
There are no fish here at all.

111
00:13:33,960 --> 00:13:34,960
Right, just come inside with me first.

112
00:13:34,960 --> 00:13:36,120
I'll definitely take you catching fish later.

113
00:13:36,759 --> 00:13:37,279
Be good.

114
00:13:37,399 --> 00:13:38,120
I'll really take you.

115
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:38,799
I'm not lying to you.

116
00:13:38,799 --> 00:13:39,879
I'll really take you catching fish.

117
00:13:40,039 --> 00:13:40,519
Just follow me...

118
00:13:40,519 --> 00:13:41,039
Wang Yunsheng.

119
00:13:41,399 --> 00:13:41,720
Here!

120
00:13:42,320 --> 00:13:42,919
Who is this?

121
00:13:43,440 --> 00:13:44,919
This is Dai Mingming, the one I told you about.

122
00:13:50,320 --> 00:13:51,440
Why did you bring him here?

123
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:52,360
He confessed to everything.

124
00:13:53,159 --> 00:13:54,759
Confessed? Confessed to what?

125
00:13:55,720 --> 00:13:56,200
Well, not confessed.

126
00:13:56,200 --> 00:13:57,320
He admitted it himself.

127
00:13:57,559 --> 00:13:58,879
That night, it was his mom who...

128
00:13:59,639 --> 00:14:00,120
Mingming, Mingming.

129
00:14:00,480 --> 00:14:01,840
What did you tell me at the hospital just now?

130
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:02,519
Say it again.

131
00:14:02,519 --> 00:14:03,120
At the hospital,

132
00:14:03,120 --> 00:14:04,679
I said my mom took me catching fish.

133
00:14:05,440 --> 00:14:06,840
That's not what you said just now.

134
00:14:07,320 --> 00:14:08,720
Lying is wrong, Dai Mingming.

135
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:09,799
You just admitted it yourself.

136
00:14:09,799 --> 00:14:11,039
You said your mom pushed you into the river.

137
00:14:11,279 --> 00:14:12,320
Chief Ji, that's really what he said.

138
00:14:12,320 --> 00:14:12,960
Wang Yunsheng, come here.

139
00:14:18,159 --> 00:14:19,399
Whose idea was it to bring him here?

140
00:14:19,919 --> 00:14:20,480
Where is Li Zhi?

141
00:14:21,559 --> 00:14:22,279
M-Mine. My idea.

142
00:14:23,240 --> 00:14:23,879
Li Zhi was busy.

143
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:24,879
I went to the hospital by myself.

144
00:14:24,879 --> 00:14:26,519
Don't you know Auxiliary Police have no law enforcement authority?

145
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:28,440
I know.

146
00:14:30,039 --> 00:14:31,200
I just wanted to quickly solve this case.

147
00:14:31,200 --> 00:14:32,120
Who cares what you wanted!

148
00:14:33,039 --> 00:14:34,320
You're overstepping your authority.

149
00:14:35,519 --> 00:14:36,519
Don't take matters into your own hands from now on.

150
00:14:37,320 --> 00:14:38,519
Focus on assisting Li Zhi.

151
00:14:39,480 --> 00:14:41,080
Chief Ji, I was the one who discovered this case.

152
00:14:48,080 --> 00:14:49,639
Do you get to handle it just because you found it?

153
00:14:50,919 --> 00:14:52,240
If I really handed this case to you,

154
00:14:52,919 --> 00:14:53,879
would you know how to handle it?

155
00:14:54,600 --> 00:14:55,519
Could you even figure it out?

156
00:14:58,240 --> 00:15:00,679
Improve your own professional skills first.

157
00:15:03,440 --> 00:15:03,960
Get back to work.

158
00:15:05,159 --> 00:15:05,440
Yes, ma'am.

159
00:15:54,879 --> 00:15:56,080
Your blanket folding needs work.

160
00:15:56,279 --> 00:15:57,080
You need more practice.

161
00:15:58,240 --> 00:15:58,600
I'll practice.

162
00:15:59,279 --> 00:16:01,120
A few more folds and I'll catch up to you.

163
00:16:32,720 --> 00:16:34,039
Folded by the laundry fairy?

164
00:16:44,240 --> 00:16:45,120
Beautiful.

165
00:16:48,600 --> 00:16:49,679
How long did it take to learn this?

166
00:16:56,799 --> 00:16:57,960
Fold it like this.

167
00:16:58,080 --> 00:16:58,759
Right.

168
00:16:59,399 --> 00:16:59,919
And then?

169
00:17:00,519 --> 00:17:01,559
Then how... how do I fold it?

170
00:17:02,240 --> 00:17:03,120
Flip it over.

171
00:17:04,039 --> 00:17:06,079
And it turns into an airplane.

172
00:17:07,039 --> 00:17:07,759
Chief Liao.

173
00:17:08,039 --> 00:17:09,079
Look who's here.

174
00:17:09,279 --> 00:17:10,240
Say hello to Uncle Liao.

175
00:17:10,759 --> 00:17:11,960
Hello, Uncle Liao.

176
00:17:11,960 --> 00:17:12,440
Hello.

177
00:17:12,960 --> 00:17:14,000
Here to buy something?

178
00:17:23,240 --> 00:17:23,920
Did you fold this?

179
00:17:24,400 --> 00:17:25,680
My mom folded it for me.

180
00:17:26,160 --> 00:17:26,920
Your mom is awesome.

181
00:17:32,720 --> 00:17:33,079
Here.

182
00:17:34,039 --> 00:17:35,640
Last time you gave me a certificate.

183
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:37,359
I have a little gift for you.

184
00:17:38,039 --> 00:17:39,039
To return the favor.

185
00:17:40,079 --> 00:17:41,240
Do you know what this is?

186
00:17:45,720 --> 00:17:47,039
Then do you know what this is?

187
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:48,839
A gun.

188
00:17:49,319 --> 00:17:50,279
So think about it.

189
00:17:51,319 --> 00:17:51,960
What is this?

190
00:17:57,880 --> 00:17:58,799
A bullet casing.

191
00:18:04,160 --> 00:18:05,519
Let me put it on you.

192
00:18:07,559 --> 00:18:09,440
This is from when I joined the Special Police Unit,

193
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:12,559
the bullet casing from my first bullseye.

194
00:18:14,079 --> 00:18:15,839
Once you wear it, you won't be afraid of anything.

195
00:18:16,440 --> 00:18:17,000
Little man.

196
00:18:21,079 --> 00:18:22,279
Quick, thank Uncle Liao.

197
00:18:22,680 --> 00:18:24,079
Thank you, Uncle Liao.

198
00:18:27,200 --> 00:18:29,160
Dad, the balloon popped.

199
00:18:32,960 --> 00:18:33,359
Sit down.

200
00:18:33,839 --> 00:18:34,160
Sit.

201
00:18:34,519 --> 00:18:34,880
Come on.

202
00:18:35,519 --> 00:18:36,200
Breathe in.

203
00:18:39,319 --> 00:18:39,880
Breathe in.

204
00:18:40,599 --> 00:18:41,119
Breathe in.

205
00:18:42,839 --> 00:18:44,279
Okay, it's alright.

206
00:18:45,359 --> 00:18:45,680
Sweetie.

207
00:18:46,279 --> 00:18:47,160
Dad will buy you a new one.

208
00:18:48,839 --> 00:18:49,599
How about we buy this one?

209
00:18:50,279 --> 00:18:50,680
Let's buy two more.

210
00:19:09,240 --> 00:19:09,839
Is it good?

211
00:19:15,359 --> 00:19:16,440
I'll take you to get your hair washed later.

212
00:19:16,599 --> 00:19:17,319
We'll stay here tonight.

213
00:19:20,359 --> 00:19:20,680
No.

214
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:23,240
Back to the hospital, then?

215
00:19:24,480 --> 00:19:25,079
I want to go home.

216
00:19:49,799 --> 00:19:50,240
Take a look.

217
00:19:51,359 --> 00:19:52,039
Which one do you want to drink?

218
00:20:17,160 --> 00:20:17,799
Dai Mingming,

219
00:20:19,240 --> 00:20:20,240
that day, did your mom

220
00:20:20,279 --> 00:20:21,759
really take you to catch fish?

221
00:20:26,759 --> 00:20:28,599
That day, Mom said she was taking me away.

222
00:20:32,839 --> 00:20:34,039
She said we were going to catch fish.

223
00:20:34,119 --> 00:20:34,960
I was so happy.

224
00:20:35,839 --> 00:20:36,720
The water tasted awful,

225
00:20:36,720 --> 00:20:37,519
and it was so cold.

226
00:20:38,279 --> 00:20:40,599
Then I... I just fell in.

227
00:20:40,599 --> 00:20:42,359
Then my mom came in too.

228
00:20:44,200 --> 00:20:47,000
Finally, the police officers pulled us out.

229
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:48,960
And after they pulled us out, it got even colder.

230
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:51,720
We were soaking wet.

231
00:20:59,000 --> 00:20:59,359
Chief!

232
00:21:00,960 --> 00:21:01,839
Dai Mingming's mom is here.

233
00:21:07,519 --> 00:21:08,039
Mom!

234
00:21:08,279 --> 00:21:08,759
Mom!

235
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:12,519
Drink.

236
00:21:13,720 --> 00:21:14,519
You have some too. Drink.

237
00:21:17,839 --> 00:21:18,400
It's so sweet.

238
00:21:25,920 --> 00:21:26,559
Chief Ji,

239
00:21:28,759 --> 00:21:29,720
I'm here to turn myself in.

240
00:21:51,240 --> 00:21:52,359
Looks like everything's fine now.

241
00:21:53,079 --> 00:21:55,640
No need to see me out. Let Naonao get some rest.

242
00:21:55,920 --> 00:21:56,759
I'm heading back.

243
00:21:57,400 --> 00:21:57,839
Bye.

244
00:21:58,480 --> 00:21:59,000
Bye.

245
00:21:59,079 --> 00:21:59,599
Bye.

246
00:22:09,279 --> 00:22:09,680
Let's go.

247
00:22:10,559 --> 00:22:11,079
Go back to sleep.

248
00:22:11,279 --> 00:22:11,519
Come on.

249
00:23:39,039 --> 00:23:39,400
You're here.

250
00:23:42,599 --> 00:23:43,119
Commissar Tan.

251
00:23:44,359 --> 00:23:45,039
Just got off work?

252
00:23:45,599 --> 00:23:46,359
Just got off work.

253
00:23:46,400 --> 00:23:47,160
Why aren't you asleep yet?

254
00:23:47,960 --> 00:23:49,160
I can't sleep.

255
00:23:50,079 --> 00:23:50,920
Just out for a stroll.

256
00:23:51,680 --> 00:23:53,319
Are you getting used to things here?

257
00:23:53,680 --> 00:23:54,160
It's pretty good.

258
00:23:59,799 --> 00:24:00,559
Your leg...

259
00:24:01,240 --> 00:24:02,440
Trained too hard?

260
00:24:03,200 --> 00:24:04,039
Just out of shape.

261
00:24:06,440 --> 00:24:08,400
You fold your blanket quite well.

262
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:10,079
I learned it in the army.

263
00:24:11,880 --> 00:24:13,599
You should teach me sometime.

264
00:24:13,960 --> 00:24:16,000
Mine always looks so shapeless.

265
00:24:17,400 --> 00:24:18,200
Really nice.

266
00:24:18,799 --> 00:24:19,400
Beautiful.

267
00:24:20,960 --> 00:24:21,839
You're not in a hurry to sleep, are you?

268
00:24:22,240 --> 00:24:22,839
No rush.

269
00:24:23,240 --> 00:24:24,599
Grab a chair, let's chat.

270
00:24:25,079 --> 00:24:25,440
Yes, sir.

271
00:24:34,680 --> 00:24:35,519
You seem a bit down.

272
00:24:36,279 --> 00:24:37,039
Feeling wronged?

273
00:24:37,759 --> 00:24:38,160
No.

274
00:24:39,000 --> 00:24:40,200
I don't buy it.

275
00:24:40,359 --> 00:24:41,440
You think I can't tell?

276
00:24:42,079 --> 00:24:43,480
All those years as a political officer...

277
00:24:43,759 --> 00:24:44,319
...would have been for nothing.

278
00:24:46,400 --> 00:24:47,319
Your boss scolded you, huh?

279
00:24:49,319 --> 00:24:49,880
Why was it?

280
00:24:51,240 --> 00:24:52,160
Even if my boss scolded me...

281
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:53,599
...I still want to stay at the station.

282
00:24:54,680 --> 00:24:56,400
No one's stopping you from staying.

283
00:24:56,720 --> 00:24:57,839
What are you so nervous about?

284
00:24:58,400 --> 00:24:59,799
We're just chatting.

285
00:25:06,119 --> 00:25:06,559
Yunsheng.

286
00:25:07,240 --> 00:25:08,559
I think you're a pretty steady guy.

287
00:25:10,680 --> 00:25:11,720
When your boss scolds you...

288
00:25:12,720 --> 00:25:14,720
...maybe you should look for your own faults too.

289
00:25:17,440 --> 00:25:18,359
Let me help you analyze it.

290
00:25:19,079 --> 00:25:19,440
Okay.

291
00:25:20,799 --> 00:25:21,319
What happened?

292
00:25:22,599 --> 00:25:25,000
There was a case I discovered earlier.

293
00:25:26,039 --> 00:25:27,599
But later, Chief Ji took me off it.

294
00:25:29,519 --> 00:25:30,400
I know I'm Auxiliary Police...

295
00:25:30,400 --> 00:25:31,240
...and have no law enforcement authority.

296
00:25:32,400 --> 00:25:33,759
I just felt something was off about this case.

297
00:25:34,720 --> 00:25:36,160
So I brought the person from the hospital to the station.

298
00:25:36,160 --> 00:25:37,039
And Chief Ji got mad.

299
00:25:40,720 --> 00:25:42,160
So you feel wronged about it.

300
00:25:42,799 --> 00:25:43,599
I can understand that.

301
00:25:45,599 --> 00:25:46,680
I've been there myself.

302
00:25:50,119 --> 00:25:50,599
Do you...

303
00:25:50,599 --> 00:25:52,480
...want to hear my analysis?

304
00:25:53,079 --> 00:25:53,519
Yes.

305
00:25:55,920 --> 00:25:58,119
In terms of rules and procedures...

306
00:25:59,440 --> 00:26:00,799
...you were indeed in the wrong.

307
00:26:02,440 --> 00:26:04,720
Chief Ji was right to scold you.

308
00:26:05,079 --> 00:26:05,640
Do you admit that?

309
00:26:05,960 --> 00:26:06,319
I do.

310
00:26:10,000 --> 00:26:10,480
Your Chief Ji...

311
00:26:10,480 --> 00:26:12,519
...has she been in a really bad mood lately?

312
00:26:13,559 --> 00:26:14,759
She always seems like that.

313
00:26:14,839 --> 00:26:15,599
So cold.

314
00:26:15,720 --> 00:26:16,440
She rarely smiles.

315
00:26:21,240 --> 00:26:22,480
But Chief Ji is actually a pretty good person.

316
00:26:29,119 --> 00:26:30,160
My butt...

317
00:26:30,319 --> 00:26:30,759
Careful now.

318
00:26:32,799 --> 00:26:34,400
That stings.

319
00:26:38,720 --> 00:26:41,480
Even though Chief Ji and I are married,

320
00:26:42,839 --> 00:26:44,000
let's just stick to the facts.

321
00:26:47,279 --> 00:26:48,480
Yunsheng, I feel that...

322
00:26:48,519 --> 00:26:51,319
You... you have to learn about your leader's...

323
00:26:51,720 --> 00:26:52,839
personality and temper...

324
00:26:53,440 --> 00:26:54,160
and understand them.

325
00:26:54,559 --> 00:26:55,240
Chief Ji.

326
00:26:55,519 --> 00:26:57,839
You need to judge and analyze her objectively.

327
00:26:58,119 --> 00:26:59,000
How else will you improve?

328
00:26:59,359 --> 00:27:00,920
Don't you want to stay at the station?

329
00:27:00,920 --> 00:27:02,039
Can't you figure this out?

330
00:27:03,640 --> 00:27:04,240
Go ahead, tell me.

331
00:27:06,920 --> 00:27:08,319
Chief Ji is a good person,

332
00:27:08,920 --> 00:27:10,599
but she's a bit hard to figure out.

333
00:27:10,599 --> 00:27:11,880
I... I don't get her either.

334
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:12,960
I've been married to her for so many years,

335
00:27:12,960 --> 00:27:13,680
and a lot of the time,

336
00:27:14,279 --> 00:27:15,119
I still don't understand her.

337
00:27:15,519 --> 00:27:16,960
Matters big and small at the station,

338
00:27:16,960 --> 00:27:18,039
she handles them all herself.

339
00:27:18,039 --> 00:27:19,119
She has to control everything,

340
00:27:19,119 --> 00:27:21,160
and she takes everything upon herself.

341
00:27:21,160 --> 00:27:22,839
It's as if the whole world is her responsibility.

342
00:27:23,200 --> 00:27:23,680
Sometimes,

343
00:27:23,680 --> 00:27:25,359
I even feel like she doesn't care about others' feelings.

344
00:27:25,359 --> 00:27:26,160
She really doesn't care.

345
00:27:26,519 --> 00:27:28,319
And in how she handles certain things,

346
00:27:29,000 --> 00:27:29,799
I feel like she's unfair.

347
00:27:29,799 --> 00:27:30,960
She tends to be unfair.

348
00:27:31,319 --> 00:27:32,279
And she's emotional.

349
00:27:32,799 --> 00:27:34,480
She's especially hard on herself.

350
00:27:34,759 --> 00:27:37,000
It's hard for her to listen to anyone.

351
00:27:37,000 --> 00:27:38,319
And she can't see the good in others.

352
00:27:38,319 --> 00:27:40,680
She thinks she's right about everything.

353
00:27:40,720 --> 00:27:41,160
I'm sorry.

354
00:27:41,160 --> 00:27:41,519
I just acted on my own.

355
00:27:41,519 --> 00:27:42,160
I'm sorry, Commissar Tan.

356
00:27:42,440 --> 00:27:43,200
It's mainly my fault.

357
00:27:43,559 --> 00:27:44,640
I was only on secondment there,

358
00:27:44,640 --> 00:27:45,559
and I'm just an Auxiliary Police officer.

359
00:27:45,559 --> 00:27:46,559
Plus, I violated the rules.

360
00:27:46,640 --> 00:27:47,640
It's normal for Chief Ji to reprimand me.

361
00:27:50,039 --> 00:27:50,759
Young.

362
00:27:53,279 --> 00:27:54,160
You're too young.

363
00:27:55,440 --> 00:27:56,000
Yunsheng,

364
00:27:57,920 --> 00:28:00,039
you just arrived at a grassroots station.

365
00:28:00,799 --> 00:28:02,759
Learning takes time.

366
00:28:03,720 --> 00:28:06,799
Doesn't your leader, Chief Ji, understand this?

367
00:28:07,599 --> 00:28:09,680
Shouldn't she be more tolerant of you?

368
00:28:11,039 --> 00:28:13,079
Making progress takes time, after all.

369
00:28:13,880 --> 00:28:16,559
Whether you're regular or Auxiliary Police,

370
00:28:16,559 --> 00:28:18,160
the work objective is the same.

371
00:28:18,559 --> 00:28:19,599
To keep the community safe.

372
00:28:21,400 --> 00:28:22,640
If her unfairness toward you

373
00:28:22,640 --> 00:28:23,880
is based on this situation,

374
00:28:24,640 --> 00:28:26,880
then I need to have a good talk with your Chief Ji.

375
00:28:27,839 --> 00:28:29,000
Talk to her with facts and reason.

376
00:28:30,519 --> 00:28:32,359
You really need to take this case's

377
00:28:32,359 --> 00:28:33,359
specific details

378
00:28:33,559 --> 00:28:34,839
and explain them to me.

379
00:28:38,240 --> 00:28:38,599
Go on.

380
00:28:41,799 --> 00:28:42,359
Dai Yumei,

381
00:28:43,559 --> 00:28:44,920
let me confirm this with you one last time.

382
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:47,400
On the 27th at 6:00 p.m.,

383
00:28:48,160 --> 00:28:49,240
under the guise of catching fish,

384
00:28:49,240 --> 00:28:50,680
you lured Dai Mingming to the river,

385
00:28:51,200 --> 00:28:52,640
and then pushed him in with your own hands.

386
00:28:54,079 --> 00:28:54,799
Is this correct?

387
00:28:57,440 --> 00:28:57,920
Yes.

388
00:29:01,079 --> 00:29:02,559
Do you have anything else to confess?

389
00:29:06,119 --> 00:29:06,559
No.

390
00:29:17,960 --> 00:29:18,799
Can you talk about it?

391
00:29:19,359 --> 00:29:20,240
What were you thinking?

392
00:29:25,880 --> 00:29:26,519
I'm sick.

393
00:29:28,359 --> 00:29:29,359
I don't have much time left.

394
00:29:30,599 --> 00:29:33,400
I just didn't want to leave him alone

395
00:29:34,599 --> 00:29:35,200
in this world

396
00:29:36,039 --> 00:29:36,680
to suffer.

397
00:29:38,640 --> 00:29:39,960
You could've sent him to a welfare home.

398
00:29:40,960 --> 00:29:42,799
There are also special institutions you can apply to.

399
00:29:42,799 --> 00:29:43,640
I tried.

400
00:29:44,440 --> 00:29:45,119
I tried everything.

401
00:29:46,720 --> 00:29:47,599
Mingming is special.

402
00:29:48,480 --> 00:29:49,759
He's not like other children.

403
00:29:54,039 --> 00:29:56,279
He can't live with people he doesn't know.

404
00:29:58,079 --> 00:29:58,960
When he can't see me,

405
00:30:00,079 --> 00:30:01,119
he throws tantrums.

406
00:30:05,160 --> 00:30:05,960
Before,

407
00:30:06,680 --> 00:30:08,039
I sent him to a welfare home.

408
00:30:09,559 --> 00:30:10,640
But when he couldn't find me,

409
00:30:12,559 --> 00:30:13,400
he panicked.

410
00:30:15,559 --> 00:30:16,920
From the upper floor of the welfare home,

411
00:30:17,279 --> 00:30:18,640
he jumped out the window.

412
00:30:20,759 --> 00:30:22,240
He broke his legs.

413
00:30:27,319 --> 00:30:28,200
What about your family?

414
00:30:29,759 --> 00:30:30,519
Don't you have any relatives?

415
00:30:31,920 --> 00:30:33,759
Someone Dai Mingming could accept,

416
00:30:33,759 --> 00:30:35,960
or someone who could... accept him?

417
00:30:40,680 --> 00:30:42,920
We haven't kept in touch with our relatives.

418
00:30:44,519 --> 00:30:45,200
Actually, I...

419
00:30:45,400 --> 00:30:49,000
I had thought about entrusting him to relatives.

420
00:30:50,200 --> 00:30:50,720
But...

421
00:30:51,680 --> 00:30:52,680
later I found out

422
00:30:54,920 --> 00:30:56,880
that the ones willing to take him

423
00:30:58,640 --> 00:30:59,880
were only after my apartment.

424
00:31:06,880 --> 00:31:07,319
Tell me,

425
00:31:07,319 --> 00:31:08,759
with relatives like that,

426
00:31:10,480 --> 00:31:12,680
how could I trust them with my child?

427
00:31:19,599 --> 00:31:21,119
There must be other ways.

428
00:31:22,680 --> 00:31:23,799
It shouldn't have come to this.

429
00:31:25,559 --> 00:31:26,839
Being alive is better than anything.

430
00:31:29,759 --> 00:31:30,119
Yes...

431
00:31:33,119 --> 00:31:34,359
Being alive is better than anything.

432
00:31:37,519 --> 00:31:38,400
I know that too.

433
00:31:40,519 --> 00:31:42,240
But if I weren't truly out of options,

434
00:31:43,960 --> 00:31:44,960
tell me, what mother

435
00:31:46,079 --> 00:31:47,839
would want to harm her own child?

436
00:31:55,799 --> 00:31:57,599
I just don't know...

437
00:31:58,880 --> 00:32:00,279
if I'm gone,

438
00:32:02,440 --> 00:32:04,319
leaving Mingming all alone,

439
00:32:07,200 --> 00:32:08,799
how will he survive?

440
00:32:20,480 --> 00:32:21,359
I just thought

441
00:32:23,799 --> 00:32:24,400
if we left together,

442
00:32:27,400 --> 00:32:28,119
we'd be free.

443
00:32:52,480 --> 00:32:53,839
When you get to the final step,

444
00:32:54,279 --> 00:32:55,039
you just need to take

445
00:32:55,559 --> 00:32:57,200
the section between your palms,

446
00:32:57,200 --> 00:32:58,680
keep it roughly two fists wide,

447
00:32:58,680 --> 00:32:59,480
or about a twenty-centimeter distance.

448
00:33:00,079 --> 00:33:00,480
Fall in!

449
00:33:00,839 --> 00:33:01,359
Hurry up! Hurry up!

450
00:33:02,599 --> 00:33:03,119
Fall in!

451
00:33:06,359 --> 00:33:08,079
It was after the balloon popped

452
00:33:08,079 --> 00:33:09,240
that Naonao suddenly got scared.

453
00:33:09,839 --> 00:33:12,160
I think the gunshot from the hostage incident

454
00:33:12,200 --> 00:33:13,079
triggered him.

455
00:33:13,079 --> 00:33:13,759
It's possible.

456
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:15,440
In psychology, it's

457
00:33:15,440 --> 00:33:16,720
called gunshot stress response.

458
00:33:17,480 --> 00:33:18,920
Then we should find a professional

459
00:33:18,920 --> 00:33:20,279
to give him some psychological counseling.

460
00:33:20,920 --> 00:33:22,839
The Municipal Bureau does have a Psychological Counseling Room,

461
00:33:22,839 --> 00:33:24,160
but it's not open to the public.

462
00:33:25,279 --> 00:33:26,480
I'll put in a request later.

463
00:33:26,759 --> 00:33:28,279
Besides, this involves our Special Police Unit.

464
00:33:29,240 --> 00:33:29,480
At ease!

465
00:33:30,640 --> 00:33:30,920
Attention!

466
00:33:32,920 --> 00:33:33,640
Chief!

467
00:33:33,920 --> 00:33:35,440
Assembly complete. Awaiting your orders.

468
00:33:37,039 --> 00:33:37,799
Where's Commissar Tan?

469
00:33:41,519 --> 00:33:41,799
Tan...

470
00:33:48,559 --> 00:33:49,200
Commissar Tan said

471
00:33:49,960 --> 00:33:50,960
that today he's going to personally

472
00:33:51,160 --> 00:33:52,880
inspect the cafeteria's food safety,

473
00:33:53,920 --> 00:33:54,839
so he won't be joining the training.

474
00:33:55,160 --> 00:33:56,640
Is there an issue with the food safety?

475
00:34:07,160 --> 00:34:08,480
He'll be ruined if he keeps training.

476
00:34:09,719 --> 00:34:10,920
It's the perfect excuse to step down.

477
00:34:12,079 --> 00:34:13,400
Let's just tell him to sit this out.

478
00:34:15,840 --> 00:34:16,239
Alright.

479
00:34:18,519 --> 00:34:19,440
It's a good thing he isn't coming.

480
00:34:19,519 --> 00:34:20,480
Saves us the embarrassment.

481
00:34:21,599 --> 00:34:22,119
Let's start.

482
00:34:25,239 --> 00:34:25,519
Attention!

483
00:34:26,599 --> 00:34:27,280
Left face!

484
00:34:28,280 --> 00:34:29,960
Column left! Double time, march!

485
00:34:30,360 --> 00:34:31,360
Left, right, left!

486
00:34:31,639 --> 00:34:32,760
Iron-blooded Special Police!

487
00:34:32,960 --> 00:34:35,440
Iron-blooded Special Police, loyal guardians!

488
00:34:35,679 --> 00:34:38,280
Scaling new heights, achieving new glory!

489
00:34:51,880 --> 00:34:53,599
Thank God. I really don't want to train.

490
00:34:56,519 --> 00:34:58,079
Come on, help me think of something.

491
00:34:59,440 --> 00:35:00,840
I'm under so much pressure right now.

492
00:35:01,960 --> 00:35:03,119
I can't sleep at night.

493
00:35:03,119 --> 00:35:04,559
That guy keeps snoring.

494
00:35:05,159 --> 00:35:08,239
Then 10-kilometer runs by day, plus random extra training.

495
00:35:09,440 --> 00:35:12,239
Right now, mentally and physically,

496
00:35:13,000 --> 00:35:14,199
I am completely exhausted.

497
00:35:15,480 --> 00:35:16,599
I can barely hold on.

498
00:35:18,079 --> 00:35:18,960
Think of something.

499
00:35:23,360 --> 00:35:24,320
Seriously, Lao Tan,

500
00:35:24,320 --> 00:35:25,639
what were you thinking?

501
00:35:26,039 --> 00:35:26,960
You're an office guy,

502
00:35:26,960 --> 00:35:28,599
yet you really act like you're special ops.

503
00:35:30,000 --> 00:35:31,239
At your age, too.

504
00:35:34,800 --> 00:35:39,960
I was just trying to get things moving quickly.

505
00:35:43,719 --> 00:35:45,440
Look, wanting to fit in is fine.

506
00:35:45,960 --> 00:35:47,639
But you have to use the right approach.

507
00:35:48,719 --> 00:35:50,039
With your limited skills,

508
00:35:50,039 --> 00:35:52,440
trying to win hearts by sharing their hardship...

509
00:35:53,440 --> 00:35:54,599
I don't think it'll work.

510
00:35:57,519 --> 00:35:58,920
Lao Na is right about this.

511
00:35:59,719 --> 00:36:01,920
The Special Police Unit isn't something

512
00:36:01,920 --> 00:36:03,039
you can win over just by suffering with them.

513
00:36:04,119 --> 00:36:04,920
Besides,

514
00:36:05,039 --> 00:36:06,920
this isn't what you're good at, Tan Yan.

515
00:36:10,559 --> 00:36:11,199
This is what they call

516
00:36:11,239 --> 00:36:13,400
using your weakness against their strength.

517
00:36:20,559 --> 00:36:22,119
That last sentence just gave me an idea.

518
00:36:23,119 --> 00:36:27,239
Right. I need to use my strength against their weakness.

519
00:37:14,639 --> 00:37:16,400
Tan Yan, can you please change

520
00:37:16,599 --> 00:37:18,039
your self-centered attitude?

521
00:37:18,320 --> 00:37:19,679
From the moment you walked in,

522
00:37:19,760 --> 00:37:21,719
all you can think of is Chief Guo, the Special Police Unit,

523
00:37:21,920 --> 00:37:24,000
and your future. Do you even care about us?

524
00:38:21,320 --> 00:38:23,119
Slip your shoes on.

525
00:38:23,360 --> 00:38:23,880
Great job.

526
00:38:26,719 --> 00:38:27,480
There, all done.

527
00:38:28,679 --> 00:38:29,199
All set.

528
00:38:29,199 --> 00:38:30,880
Hello, welcome.

529
00:38:31,519 --> 00:38:32,079
Just a moment!

530
00:38:34,719 --> 00:38:35,239
Coming!

531
00:38:36,719 --> 00:38:37,400
Sorry about that.

532
00:38:37,400 --> 00:38:38,960
We aren't officially open yet.

533
00:38:47,159 --> 00:38:47,880
Are you okay?

534
00:38:55,159 --> 00:38:55,960
Still mad at me?

535
00:39:05,480 --> 00:39:06,480
This temper of yours...

536
00:39:07,599 --> 00:39:08,599
Can't you change it?

537
00:39:14,599 --> 00:39:15,039
Where's Naonao?

538
00:39:21,920 --> 00:39:22,360
Naonao!

539
00:39:24,679 --> 00:39:25,079
Naonao!

540
00:39:26,840 --> 00:39:27,239
Naonao!

541
00:39:29,360 --> 00:39:29,639
Come here.

542
00:39:34,559 --> 00:39:35,639
Why are you standing over there?

543
00:39:36,519 --> 00:39:36,800
Come here.

544
00:39:37,880 --> 00:39:38,599
Let Daddy give you a hug.

545
00:39:39,519 --> 00:39:39,760
Come on.

546
00:39:59,920 --> 00:40:01,119
This self-built house

547
00:40:01,760 --> 00:40:02,440
gets damp easily.

548
00:40:02,840 --> 00:40:03,519
And it's so small.

549
00:40:04,760 --> 00:40:06,000
It's not good for Naonao's health.

550
00:40:09,119 --> 00:40:10,519
No matter how mad you are at me,

551
00:40:12,280 --> 00:40:13,639
we can't let our child suffer, right?

552
00:40:15,239 --> 00:40:16,800
Besides, it's so dangerous out there.

553
00:40:17,280 --> 00:40:18,599
Something terrible almost happened.

554
00:40:19,960 --> 00:40:20,920
Do you know how worried I was?

555
00:40:29,719 --> 00:40:30,199
Naonao.

556
00:40:32,880 --> 00:40:33,840
Do you miss Daddy?

557
00:40:37,119 --> 00:40:38,280
Let's go home together, okay?

558
00:40:40,119 --> 00:40:40,559
Let's go home.

559
00:40:40,559 --> 00:40:41,599
We're not going back.

560
00:40:43,000 --> 00:40:44,039
This is our home now.

561
00:40:55,039 --> 00:40:56,440
It's only a home when we're together.

562
00:41:04,400 --> 00:41:05,039
Lu Haifeng,

563
00:41:05,599 --> 00:41:06,480
I don't owe you anymore.

564
00:41:08,239 --> 00:41:09,760
Where I take the child from now on,

565
00:41:09,840 --> 00:41:11,920
and how we live is none of your business.

566
00:41:16,719 --> 00:41:17,440
Are you pushing me?

567
00:41:17,440 --> 00:41:18,639
You're the one pushing me!

568
00:41:27,559 --> 00:41:28,079
Dayong,

569
00:41:30,760 --> 00:41:31,239
step outside.

570
00:41:38,079 --> 00:41:39,679
If anything happens to us here,

571
00:41:40,760 --> 00:41:41,719
none of you will get away with it.

572
00:41:48,920 --> 00:41:51,000
Do you really think living opposite the Special Police Unit

573
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:52,639
means I can't do anything to you?

574
00:41:53,760 --> 00:41:54,320
Let me tell you,

575
00:41:55,840 --> 00:41:57,360
I have a hundred ways

576
00:41:58,559 --> 00:42:00,320
to take you and Naonao away from here.

577
00:42:00,320 --> 00:42:01,000
Do you believe me?

578
00:42:03,519 --> 00:42:04,239
I believe you.

579
00:42:06,519 --> 00:42:07,440
But this shop

580
00:42:08,239 --> 00:42:11,119
is within range of the Special Police Unit's gate cameras.

581
00:42:12,760 --> 00:42:15,280
They'll also have a hundred ways to find you.

582
00:43:15,599 --> 00:43:16,360
That's a new record.

583
00:43:16,480 --> 00:43:17,480
0.8 seconds faster.

584
00:43:17,800 --> 00:43:19,639
We're strengthening our bodies

585
00:43:20,039 --> 00:43:21,840
while elevating our minds.

586
00:43:22,400 --> 00:43:24,400
Submit a thought report every three days.

587
00:43:26,320 --> 00:43:27,920
If you really want the team's respect,

588
00:43:28,119 --> 00:43:29,119
do something practical.

589
00:43:29,519 --> 00:43:31,239
Tell me, what counts as practical?

590
00:43:31,639 --> 00:43:32,920
We rented a room across the street.

591
00:43:33,639 --> 00:43:34,519
I'm warning you,

592
00:43:35,079 --> 00:43:35,719
don't go looking for trouble.
